"notes": "Modified cash basis school district; governmental funds only (Nutrition and Activities are in Other Governmental Funds). Receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (p3); beginning/ending balances p4 (fund balance = cash, CDs and county treasurer cash). Net transfers are zero in the total column (General -40,162, other funds +40,162; cross-checked: General transfers out 75,000 to Nutrition 25,000 and Activities 50,000, transfer in 34,838 from Cooperative), so transfers_in/out are null. Nonrevenue receipts 100,544 (General 51,277 = property sale 2,350 + insurance 18,175 + other 30,752; other funds 49,267 = Nutrition other 14,200 + Cooperative other 35,067) kept as other with review. Balance sheet uses the cash-basis Statement of Activities and Net Position (p2); no liabilities printed. Detail: the General Fund budget-and-actual schedule (pp7-10) is recorded rather than the General Fund components combining schedule (pp5-6), to avoid double counting; its GF total receipts 8,119,559 include transfer in 34,838 and total disbursements 7,637,187 include transfer out 75,000 (both shown as other financing). Lines with blank actual (3535 revenue, 3551 revenue, 4512, budget-only Other and Transfers budget) are omitted. General Fund spending is by program with no object breakdown (not itemized); the Exhibit N object schedule is not in the trimmed PDF. Depreciation fund printed a blank transfer line; its roll-forward ties (444,453 + 18,088 - 46,000 = 416,541). Statement p3 reclassifies private/state categorical and federal programs to Instruction; detail follows that. Printed GF budget schedule disbursement lines (pp9-10, re-read) sum to 7,559,489 excluding the 75,000 transfer (7,634,489 with it), 2,698 less than the printed total 7,637,187; the gap is in Central services (p9 lines 2510 129,408 + 2560 3,720 = 133,128 vs 135,826 on pp3/6), so the page itself does not add up (recorded in report_discrepancies). Statement line Capital outlay 1,373,033 (p3) is split into debt service principal 967,538 and debt service interest 156,829 (Special Building schedule p15) and remaining capital outlay 248,666. Read pages 1-18 of 18 Statement line Student support services 1,073,533 (p3) is split by its printed fund columns: General Fund 650,975 support services; Other Governmental Funds 422,558 student activities (Activities Fund 422,547 plus Cooperative 11)."
